<page>
  <p>
  Simple <term> linear regression </term> is a statistical method used to model the relationship 
  between a single independent variable and a continuous dependent variable. 
  By fitting a straight line of best fit to the observed data, this technique allows 
  you to visualize and predict trends. 
</p>

<p>
  The equation of this regression line is typically expressed as a linear function in 
  the form <m>y = mx + b</m>, where <m>m</m> represents the slope of the line and 
  <m>b</m> represents the y-intercept.
</p>

<exercise>  <myopenmath problem="23919"/> </exercise>
